	"body_html": "<p>I've built a handful of <a href=\"https://dev.to/madsstoumann/colors-are-math-how-they-match-and-how-to-build-a-color-picker-4ei8\">color pickers</a> through the years, so when I <a href=\"https://www.amazon.co.uk/Designers-Dictionary-Colour-Sean-Adams/dp/1419726390/?_encoding=UTF8&amp;pd_rd_w=hVrHi&amp;pf_rd_p=511c9d46-9b08-4a49-8274-fd2b88a7304c&amp;pf_rd_r=YN45PC380BHWB986M602&amp;pd_rd_r=d1d239a3-1b36-4095-b612-0012c7a979ee&amp;pd_rd_wg=iVQvL&amp;ref_=pd_gw_ci_mcx_mr_hp_d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">in this book</a> stumbled upon a color-wheel with “built-in” shades and tints, I had to code it:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"assets/672378/7f490dc3.jpg\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"assets/672378/7f490dc3.jpg\" alt=\"Color Wheel with tints and shades\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"800\" height=\"803\"></a></p>\n\n<p>At first, I thought: “That's easy – it's just a conical gradient with <em>hard stops</em> for the colors, and a radial gradient for the tints and shades”.</p>\n\n<p>But, alas, look at how “un-crisp” the edges in the conical gradient are (Chrome, MacOS):</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"assets/672378/fc06be09.jpg\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"assets/672378/fc06be09.jpg\" alt=\"Color Wheel, using conical gradient\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\"></a></p>\n\n<p>So – I had to do it in <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code>.</p>\n\n<p>Each “ring” in the circle is built up by 12 circles with different colors and <code>stroke-dasharray</code>:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight xml\"><code><span class=\"nt\">&lt;g</span> <span class=\"na\">id=</span><span class=\"s\">\"wheel\"</span><span class=\"nt\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"nt\">&lt;circle</span> <span class=\"na\">class=</span><span class=\"s\">\"c3\"</span> <span class=\"na\">cx=</span><span class=\"s\">\"16\"</span> <span class=\"na\">cy=</span><span class=\"s\">\"16\"</span> <span class=\"na\">r=</span><span class=\"s\">\"16\"</span><span class=\"nt\">&gt;&lt;/circle&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"nt\">&lt;circle</span> <span class=\"na\">class=</span><span class=\"s\">\"c2\"</span> <span class=\"na\">cx=</span><span class=\"s\">\"16\"</span> <span class=\"na\">cy=</span><span class=\"s\">\"16\"</span> <span class=\"na\">r=</span><span class=\"s\">\"16\"</span><span class=\"nt\">&gt;&lt;/circle&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"nt\">&lt;circle</span> <span class=\"na\">class=</span><span class=\"s\">\"c1\"</span> <span class=\"na\">cx=</span><span class=\"s\">\"16\"</span> <span class=\"na\">cy=</span><span class=\"s\">\"16\"</span> <span class=\"na\">r=</span><span class=\"s\">\"16\"</span><span class=\"nt\">&gt;&lt;/circle&gt;</span>\n...etc\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>And the CSS:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight css\"><code><span class=\"nt\">--u</span><span class=\"o\">:</span> <span class=\"nt\">calc</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"err\">100</span> <span class=\"o\">/</span> <span class=\"err\">12</span><span class=\"o\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"nc\">.c1</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"py\">stroke</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">hsl</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">--s</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">--l</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n  <span class=\"py\">stroke-dasharray</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">--u</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"m\">100</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"nc\">.c2</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"py\">stroke</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">hsl</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">30</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">--s</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">--l</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n  <span class=\"py\">stroke-dasharray</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">calc</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">2</span> <span class=\"err\">*</span> <span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">--u</span><span class=\"p\">))</span> <span class=\"m\">100</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"nc\">.c3</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"py\">stroke</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">hsl</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">60</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">--s</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">--l</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n  <span class=\"py\">stroke-dasharray</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">calc</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">3</span> <span class=\"err\">*</span> <span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">--u</span><span class=\"p\">))</span> <span class=\"m\">100</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"c\">/* ... etc */</span>\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>The circles are wrapped in a <code>&lt;g&gt;</code>-tag with <code>id=\"wheel\"</code>, so I can use <code>&lt;use&gt;</code> (pun intended) to clone the rings:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight xml\"><code><span class=\"nt\">&lt;use</span> <span class=\"na\">href=</span><span class=\"s\">\"#wheel\"</span> <span class=\"na\">class=</span><span class=\"s\">\"r3\"</span> <span class=\"nt\">/&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"nt\">&lt;use</span> <span class=\"na\">href=</span><span class=\"s\">\"#wheel\"</span> <span class=\"na\">class=</span><span class=\"s\">\"r2\"</span> <span class=\"nt\">/&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"nt\">&lt;use</span> <span class=\"na\">href=</span><span class=\"s\">\"#wheel\"</span> <span class=\"na\">class=</span><span class=\"s\">\"r1\"</span> <span class=\"nt\">/&gt;</span>\netc...\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>Each ring-class then sets a different <code>--l</code> (lightness) and <code>stroke-width</code>:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight css\"><code><span class=\"nc\">.r1</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"py\">--l</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"m\">40%</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"py\">stroke-width</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"m\">3</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"nc\">.r2</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"py\">--l</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"m\">45%</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"py\">stroke-width</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"m\">6</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"c\">/* ... etc */</span>\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>In the final result I've chosen more tints than shades, so it's not as dark as in the book-example. Firefox has issues with setting some svg-attributes in CSS, so check it out in Chrome, Edge or Safari:</p>\n\n<p><iframe height=\"600\" src=\"https://codepen.io/stoumann/embed/zYNmZMN?height=600&amp;default-tab=result&amp;embed-version=2\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" allowtransparency=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\n</iframe>\n</p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  <a name=\"lets-have-some-fun\" href=\"#lets-have-some-fun\">\n  </a>\n  Let's have some fun!\n</h2>\n\n<p>How about <strong>rotating</strong> those color rings – or changing the <strong>saturation</strong>? Scroll down to see and try the controls, if they're not at the top of the Pen:</p>\n\n<p><iframe height=\"600\" src=\"https://codepen.io/stoumann/embed/KKaGWJw?height=600&amp;default-tab=result&amp;embed-version=2\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" allowtransparency=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\n</iframe>\n</p>\n\n<p>To have an <strong>automated animation</strong>, animating the <code>--r</code> custom property, we need to register a Custom Property:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight css\"><code><span class=\"k\">@property</span> <span class=\"n\">--r</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"py\">syntax</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s1\">\"&lt;angle&gt;\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"py\">initial-value</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"m\">0deg</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"py\">inherits</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>And the animation:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight css\"><code><span class=\"k\">@keyframes</span> <span class=\"n\">rotate</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"err\">100</span><span class=\"o\">%</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"py\">--r</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"m\">360deg</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>Resulting in this (you need Chrome/Edge with Houdini):</p>\n\n<p><iframe height=\"600\" src=\"https://codepen.io/stoumann/embed/abpRJgy?height=600&amp;default-tab=result&amp;embed-version=2\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" allowtransparency=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\n</iframe>\n</p>\n\n<p>Don't stare at it too long – or you'll be hypnotized!</p>\n\n<p>Thanks for reading!</p>\n\n",
	"body_markdown": "I've built a handful of [color pickers](https://dev.to/madsstoumann/colors-are-math-how-they-match-and-how-to-build-a-color-picker-4ei8) through the years, so when I [in this book](https://www.amazon.co.uk/Designers-Dictionary-Colour-Sean-Adams/dp/1419726390/?_encoding=UTF8&pd_rd_w=hVrHi&pf_rd_p=511c9d46-9b08-4a49-8274-fd2b88a7304c&pf_rd_r=YN45PC380BHWB986M602&pd_rd_r=d1d239a3-1b36-4095-b612-0012c7a979ee&pd_rd_wg=iVQvL&ref_=pd_gw_ci_mcx_mr_hp_d) stumbled upon a color-wheel with “built-in” shades and tints, I had to code it:\n\n![Color Wheel with tints and shades](assets/672378/826cc611.jpg)\n\nAt first, I thought: “That's easy – it's just a conical gradient with *hard stops* for the colors, and a radial gradient for the tints and shades”.\n\nBut, alas, look at how “un-crisp” the edges in the conical gradient are (Chrome, MacOS):\n\n![Color Wheel, using conical gradient](assets/672378/26c6763d.png)\n\nSo – I had to do it in `<svg>`.\n\nEach “ring” in the circle is built up by 12 circles with different colors and `stroke-dasharray`:\n\n```xml\n<g id=\"wheel\">\n  <circle class=\"c3\" cx=\"16\" cy=\"16\" r=\"16\"></circle>\n  <circle class=\"c2\" cx=\"16\" cy=\"16\" r=\"16\"></circle>\n  <circle class=\"c1\" cx=\"16\" cy=\"16\" r=\"16\"></circle>\n...etc\n```\n\nAnd the CSS:\n\n```css\n--u: calc(100 / 12);\n\n.c1 {\n  stroke: hsl(0, var(--s), var(--l));\n  stroke-dasharray: var(--u) 100;\n}\n.c2 {\n  stroke: hsl(30, var(--s), var(--l));\n  stroke-dasharray: calc(2 * var(--u)) 100;\n}\n.c3 {\n  stroke: hsl(60, var(--s), var(--l));\n  stroke-dasharray: calc(3 * var(--u)) 100;\n}\n/* ... etc */\n```\nThe circles are wrapped in a `<g>`-tag with `id=\"wheel\"`, so I can use `<use>` (pun intended) to clone the rings:\n\n```xml\n<use href=\"#wheel\" class=\"r3\" />\n<use href=\"#wheel\" class=\"r2\" />\n<use href=\"#wheel\" class=\"r1\" />\netc...\n```\nEach ring-class then sets a different `--l` (lightness) and `stroke-width`:\n\n```css\n.r1 {\n  --l: 40%;\n  stroke-width: 3;\n}\n.r2 {\n  --l: 45%;\n  stroke-width: 6;\n}\n/* ... etc */\n```\n\nIn the final result I've chosen more tints than shades, so it's not as dark as in the book-example. Firefox has issues with setting some svg-attributes in CSS, so check it out in Chrome, Edge or Safari:\n\n{% codepen https://codepen.io/stoumann/pen/zYNmZMN %}\n\n---\n\n## Let's have some fun! \n\nHow about **rotating** those color rings – or changing the **saturation**? Scroll down to see and try the controls, if they're not at the top of the Pen:\n\n{% codepen https://codepen.io/stoumann/pen/KKaGWJw %}\n\nTo have an **automated animation**, animating the `--r` custom property, we need to register a Custom Property:\n\n```css\n@property --r {\n  syntax: \"<angle>\";\n  initial-value: 0deg;\n  inherits: false;\n}\n```\n\nAnd the animation:\n\n```css\n@keyframes rotate {\n  100% {\n    --r: 360deg;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nResulting in this (you need Chrome/Edge with Houdini):\n\n{% codepen https://codepen.io/stoumann/pen/abpRJgy %}\n\nDon't stare at it too long – or you'll be hypnotized!\n\nThanks for reading!\n \n \n ",
